# tp4/next-2 window: this is tp4-kvread-next-jobs/Q1-kvread-qualify re-pointed at the integrated image tp4-next2-1 (B0 of this pack, built from the tp4/next-2 head = tp4/octo-2 + tp4/prod-fixes); where the text below
# says tp4/prod-fixes or the window branch read tp4/next-2, and the image tag placeholder is tp4-next2-1 (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env). ORDER.txt of this pack has the order and the minutes.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the region-read qualification pack (tp4-kvread-next-jobs, docs/prefix-audit-cost.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the cost.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env); the image must bake the qwen_kv_read extension (the Dockerfile layer and
# provenance check (g) of the build) and carry levern_route with QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_KV_READ, so a tag built before this branch is refused by the READ rule below.
# Q1 (QUALIFY, the first card job): ttnn.qwen_read_blocks, the audits' region read (the qwen_kv_read extension baked into the image), against the whole-cache read, byte for byte, on the SERVED (1, 4) mesh
# (scripts/ci/tp4_kv_read_probe.py -> optimisation/ttnn-op/kv_region_read/kv_region_read_card.py run()): a cache of the production pool's size (19,968 blocks) allocated as production allocates its KV, five
# block sets (one block, a run of 512, scattered ids, a shuffled order, two runs), no program-cache growth, the read volume following the row, and the timing split (device read against host unpack).
# READ: the line 'KV_READ_PROBE verdict=PASS' and 'KV_READ_PROBE extension source: baked' ('mount' means the image predates the graft and the rig's directory was used). FAIL or NOT-MEASURED = the region read is
# NOT QUALIFIED: Q2, A0R and A1R are skipped (ORDER.txt NEEDS lines) and the audited jobs run as the engine-reuse and window packs wrote them (the whole-cache read, about 8.4 minutes a request).
# The probe opens the mesh once and closes it; a failed run needs a reset before the next hardware job. The box is the probe's own timeout (the workflow bounds the docker run by it): 30 minutes under the fabric step's 45.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=kvread
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=30
